1
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:47,979
[When I Meet The Moon]

2
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:50,940
[Episode 5]

3
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:55,620
Uncle.

4
00:01:57,509 --> 00:01:59,060
Thank you too.

5
00:02:07,230 --> 00:02:09,030
Uncle, what's going on?

6
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:11,910
No idea.

7
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:14,020
I've fixed everything.

8
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:14,780
I'm off.

9
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:16,070
Aren't you staying for dinner?

10
00:02:16,070 --> 00:02:16,750
No, thanks.

11
00:02:22,630 --> 00:02:23,740
Yes!

12
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,030
I finally get to

13
00:02:25,030 --> 00:02:26,250
work with you!

14
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:28,560
Thank you, thank you.

15
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,590
Hello, Mrs. Jiang.

16
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:38,590
Shize,

17
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:39,800
what should we do?

18
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:40,960
Grandma is missing.

19
00:02:41,030 --> 00:02:41,750
Your uncle and I

20
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:43,500
have been looking for her for ages,
but we still haven't found her.

21
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:44,960
Don't worry, Mrs. Jiang.

22
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:46,300
I'll be right over.

23
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:52,770
What's taking him so long?

24
00:02:52,930 --> 00:02:53,590
Mrs. Jiang.

25
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:55,020
You're finally here!

26
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:55,370
What happened?

27
00:02:55,370 --> 00:02:56,370
I'm worried sick.

28
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:58,120
Grandma and I were
at the shop this afternoon.

29
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,079
I just went inside

30
00:02:59,079 --> 00:03:00,180
to take a phone call,

31
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:01,910
and when I came back, she was gone.

32
00:03:01,910 --> 00:03:03,340
Your uncle went out looking for her,

33
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:04,910
but I still haven't heard from him.

34
00:03:04,910 --> 00:03:06,020
What if something's happened to her?

35
00:03:06,020 --> 00:03:07,340
Should we call the police?

36
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:08,310
Mrs. Jiang, I—

37
00:03:08,710 --> 00:03:09,310
Uncle.

38
00:03:09,310 --> 00:03:09,930
You're back.

39
00:03:09,930 --> 00:03:11,530
Where is she? Did you find her?

40
00:03:11,530 --> 00:03:13,120
No. She hasn't come back yet?

41
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,180
No, not yet.

42
00:03:14,710 --> 00:03:16,500
Mrs. Jiang, please don't panic.

43
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:17,020
I'll help

44
00:03:17,020 --> 00:03:17,870
look for her.

45
00:03:18,210 --> 00:03:19,240
Then I'll go too.

46
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:19,579
That's enough.

47
00:03:19,579 --> 00:03:20,810
Stay home and wait.

48
00:03:20,910 --> 00:03:21,630
If she comes back,

49
00:03:21,630 --> 00:03:22,740
call me right away.

50
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:24,740
Call me as soon as you have an update.

51
00:03:45,590 --> 00:03:46,240
Listen,

52
00:03:46,630 --> 00:03:47,470
I found this

53
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:48,910
huge open space recently.

54
00:03:48,910 --> 00:03:49,900
It's right over there,

55
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:51,400
perfect for playing soccer.

56
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:52,370
I've mastered Carlos's

57
00:03:52,370 --> 00:03:53,630
free-kick technique.

58
00:03:53,910 --> 00:03:54,520
Just wait.

59
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,650
I'm gonna show you what I can do in a bit.

60
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:07,840
Take it.

61
00:04:08,740 --> 00:04:09,200
Come on.

62
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:10,500
Get ready.

63
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:12,810
Pass it!

64
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:14,240
Take it.

65
00:04:14,710 --> 00:04:15,210
Pass it to me!

66
00:04:15,210 --> 00:04:15,870
Not bad.

67
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:17,950
Yuan.

68
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:19,240
Take it.

69
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:30,170
Yuan, Shize,

70
00:04:30,450 --> 00:04:31,220
play a little longer,

71
00:04:31,220 --> 00:04:33,020
then we'll head back for dinner.

72
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:34,560
Okay, be right there.

73
00:04:34,810 --> 00:04:35,810
Coming, Grandma.

74
00:04:58,630 --> 00:04:59,360
Yuan,

75
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:00,980
Yuan,

76
00:05:02,810 --> 00:05:04,600
why are you home so late?

77
00:05:05,690 --> 00:05:06,500
Grandma.

78
00:05:07,250 --> 00:05:08,300
Did you get held up

79
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:08,810
by all the things you had

80
00:05:08,810 --> 00:05:09,860
to do at school?

81
00:05:13,510 --> 00:05:14,420
Where's Shize?

82
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:17,160
Did Shize get into trouble again?

83
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:20,750
He's still young

84
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:23,200
and doesn't know any better.

85
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:24,560
As his elder brother,

86
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:26,220
you need to keep an eye on him.

87
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:32,220
Shize,

88
00:05:33,030 --> 00:05:33,690
why

89
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:35,280
the long face?

90
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:39,630
You were so adorable
when you were little.

91
00:05:40,010 --> 00:05:41,390
You two brothers

92
00:05:41,620 --> 00:05:43,950
were always finding ways
to make me laugh.

93
00:05:45,310 --> 00:05:46,170
But these days,

94
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:49,690
I hardly ever see you smile.

95
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,000
Kids who smile a lot

96
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:56,060
have good luck,

97
00:05:56,670 --> 00:05:58,960
so remember to smile more often.

98
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:08,830
Grandma,

99
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:12,100
let's go. I'll take you home.

100
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:13,240
Okay.

101
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:33,600
I'm gonna be late! I'm gonna be late!

102
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,490
I can't run anymore.

103
00:06:40,510 --> 00:06:41,970
Make way! Coming through!

104
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,750
Make way, make way, make way!

105
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,800
Aren't you usually glued
to your skateboard?

106
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:51,730
Finally decided to get your feet
on the ground today?

107
00:06:51,730 --> 00:06:52,659
My skateboard broke.

108
00:06:52,659 --> 00:06:53,510
I snapped it

109
00:06:53,510 --> 00:06:54,510
during practice yesterday.

110
00:06:54,510 --> 00:06:55,420
Who knows when the new one

111
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:56,680
I ordered will arrive?

112
00:06:57,070 --> 00:06:57,770
Hop on.

113
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:02,100
Hop on what?

114
00:07:02,250 --> 00:07:03,220
I'm...

115
00:07:03,510 --> 00:07:05,710
I'm getting some exercise, that's all.

116
00:07:05,810 --> 00:07:07,620
Trying to save face, huh?

117
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:08,770
You'll lose points

118
00:07:08,770 --> 00:07:09,630
if you're late.

119
00:07:11,010 --> 00:07:11,770
Then again,

120
00:07:11,810 --> 00:07:13,540
what do I care?

121
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:15,670
It's not my points they're deducting.

122
00:07:17,310 --> 00:07:18,420
Well, it's just...

123
00:07:19,070 --> 00:07:20,670
there's no seat on your bike.

124
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:22,340
How am I supposed to ride it?

125
00:07:32,510 --> 00:07:33,720
Isn't that Fu Zhengchu?

126
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:34,430
Why is Fu Zhengchu

127
00:07:34,430 --> 00:07:35,620
riding on the back of a girl's bike?

128
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:36,480
Senior Fu?

129
00:07:36,510 --> 00:07:38,440
What's going on between those two?

130
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:53,409
When's your skateboard arriving?

131
00:07:53,870 --> 00:07:55,270
Sometime later.

132
00:07:55,270 --> 00:07:56,220
Why do you ask?

133
00:07:56,860 --> 00:07:57,570
No reason.

134
00:07:57,630 --> 00:07:59,360
Let's add each other on WeChat.

135
00:07:59,570 --> 00:08:00,630
WeChat?

136
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:03,330
I could help you
if you ever need anything.

137
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:04,070
I'm running late for class.

138
00:08:04,070 --> 00:08:05,000
Maybe next time.

139
00:08:08,270 --> 00:08:09,730
Trying so hard to act cool.

140
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:17,950
Hello.

141
00:08:18,130 --> 00:08:18,690
Hello.

142
00:08:25,750 --> 00:08:26,620
Yes, yes,

143
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:28,000
they said

144
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,330
they won't have it ready until Wednesday.

145
00:08:42,270 --> 00:08:42,909
Excuse me,

146
00:08:42,909 --> 00:08:43,929
sorry to bother you.

147
00:08:43,929 --> 00:08:45,830
I'm the new intern.

148
00:08:45,910 --> 00:08:47,120
I wanted to ask

149
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:47,790
who's in charge of coordinating—

150
00:08:47,790 --> 00:08:48,410
Yun Li!

151
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:51,820
It's fine, thank you.

152
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:54,290
Jiameng.

153
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:55,430
You're here.

154
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:56,770
I'll show you to your desk.

155
00:08:56,770 --> 00:08:57,340
Okay.

156
00:08:57,340 --> 00:08:57,870
Let's go.

157
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:01,820
There are so few openings

158
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:02,940
in the Engineering Department this year,

159
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:04,010
and the competition is fierce.

160
00:09:04,010 --> 00:09:05,120
There wasn't much choice.

161
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,670
Luckily, you were willing
to join the publicity department.

162
00:09:06,670 --> 00:09:08,010
I didn't think too much about it.

163
00:09:08,010 --> 00:09:09,000
I'm just happy

164
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,120
to be at EAW.

165
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:11,370
By the way, Jiameng,

166
00:09:11,590 --> 00:09:13,790
what does the publicity department do?

167
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:15,870
Our company was
only established recently,

168
00:09:15,870 --> 00:09:16,370
and everything

169
00:09:16,370 --> 00:09:17,900
is still growing steadily.

170
00:09:18,630 --> 00:09:19,700
EAW's

171
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:20,170
KPIs

172
00:09:20,170 --> 00:09:20,840
rely heavily on the support

173
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:22,500
of the publicity department.

174
00:09:22,530 --> 00:09:23,580
So what will

175
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:25,120
my main responsibilities be?

176
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:26,170
That depends on

177
00:09:26,170 --> 00:09:27,030
what your department

178
00:09:27,030 --> 00:09:28,030
needs.

179
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:29,720
Just do your best to help out.

180
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:30,580
You might even

181
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:32,840
have to lend a hand to other departments.

182
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:36,070
So basically, I'm running errands
for everyone.

183
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,270
Well, coordination and teamwork

184
00:09:38,270 --> 00:09:39,890
are important, too.

185
00:09:40,860 --> 00:09:41,860
Here's your desk.

186
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:42,890
Okay.

187
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:43,980
Ms. Fang is still busy.

188
00:09:43,980 --> 00:09:45,100
Take some time to get familiar
with things first.

189
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:45,580
All right.

190
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:46,100
If you need anything,

191
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:47,830
feel free to come to me anytime.

192
00:09:50,670 --> 00:09:51,270
Hi, everyone.

193
00:09:51,270 --> 00:09:51,840
Hey!

194
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:52,600
What's your name?

195
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:53,250
Yun Li.

196
00:09:59,980 --> 00:10:00,770
Lili,

197
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:02,370
let's go have some fun after work

198
00:10:02,370 --> 00:10:03,220
to celebrate

199
00:10:03,220 --> 00:10:04,080
your first day!

200
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:05,620
Sure.

201
00:10:10,030 --> 00:10:11,290
See you after work.

202
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:14,600
Isn't that the girl from earlier?

203
00:10:15,630 --> 00:10:16,440
Hello,

204
00:10:16,530 --> 00:10:17,940
I'm Yunli, the new intern

205
00:10:17,940 --> 00:10:18,940
starting today.

206
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:21,100
I look forward to learning from you all.

207
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:22,870
Please let me know if there's anything
I can help with.

208
00:10:22,870 --> 00:10:23,440
Alright,

209
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:25,500
go make me a cup of coffee.

210
00:10:28,530 --> 00:10:29,100
Excuse me.

211
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:30,230
Here's your coffee.

212
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:36,440
Are you trying to scald me?

213
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:37,320
I'm sorry.

214
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:38,430
I'll make you another cup.

215
00:10:38,430 --> 00:10:39,390
Forget it, forget it.

216
00:10:39,390 --> 00:10:41,720
You can't even make
a decent cup of coffee.

217
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:42,750
Go make 50 copies

218
00:10:42,810 --> 00:10:44,000
of these documents.

219
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,030
Okay.

220
00:10:47,030 --> 00:10:47,840
I'm sorry.

221
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:52,130
Mr. Qin,

222
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,650
where's the new intern?

223
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:56,980
Right over there.

224
00:10:57,010 --> 00:10:57,940
She's so clumsy.

225
00:11:00,870 --> 00:11:01,650
Yun Li.

226
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:04,030
Ms. Fang.

227
00:11:04,030 --> 00:11:04,770
The engineering department

228
00:11:04,770 --> 00:11:06,440
needs extra hands
for equipment maintenance today.

229
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:07,950
Can you go help out with them?

230
00:11:07,950 --> 00:11:08,760
Ms. Fang,

231
00:11:09,090 --> 00:11:11,220
I've still got a pile of work to do here.

232
00:11:13,260 --> 00:11:14,070
Hey, you.

233
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,370
Go help them,

234
00:11:15,620 --> 00:11:17,880
and come straight back when you're done.

235
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:19,130
Okay.

236
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:31,870
Feifei,

237
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:34,440
why don't you come in to work today?

238
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:35,700
I can't, Mr. Qin.

239
00:11:35,730 --> 00:11:37,260
I've got things to do today.

240
00:11:37,630 --> 00:11:40,230
If you don't show up soon,
you'll lose this job.

241
00:11:54,620 --> 00:11:55,410
You're here.

242
00:12:04,050 --> 00:12:04,840
Thank you.

243
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:07,620
I mean,

244
00:12:09,250 --> 00:12:10,840
thank you for suggesting

245
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:11,750
EAW

246
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:19,150
Ms. Fang asked me to come help you.

247
00:12:19,150 --> 00:12:20,610
Is there anything I can do?

248
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:24,360
No need to be so formal.

249
00:12:30,270 --> 00:12:30,870
Let's go.

250
00:12:41,620 --> 00:12:42,420
Screwdriver.

251
00:12:48,890 --> 00:12:50,860
Did you skip breakfast?

252
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:54,000
I noticed you only had a cup of coffee
on your desk.

253
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,500
Do you usually just have coffee
for breakfast?

254
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:57,000
Yeah.

255
00:12:58,150 --> 00:12:59,440
Just having coffee for breakfast

256
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:01,040
isn't good for your stomach.

257
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:05,460
You said last time
that you liked crepe rolls.

258
00:13:05,460 --> 00:13:07,550
How about I make some
and bring them for you?

259
00:13:07,550 --> 00:13:08,360
No need.

260
00:13:12,050 --> 00:13:12,890
I heard

261
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:14,200
you've competed in

262
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:15,750
lots of robotics competitions.

263
00:13:15,750 --> 00:13:17,350
You must be really good at it.

264
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:18,390
I'm not bad.

265
00:13:19,890 --> 00:13:20,700
Actually,

266
00:13:21,220 --> 00:13:22,960
I love robots too.

267
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:25,210
I've even built one myself.

268
00:13:31,170 --> 00:13:32,200
Do you think it's weird

269
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:34,270
that I'm into robots?

270
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:37,290
No.

271
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,460
Building a robot yourself

272
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:44,700
is impressive.

273
00:13:46,390 --> 00:13:47,520
You really think so?

274
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:03,890
What should we do next?

275
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:06,640
What do you want to do?

276
00:14:06,870 --> 00:14:08,390
That's a funny question.

277
00:14:08,670 --> 00:14:10,400
Shouldn't I be asking you that?

278
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:17,100
This looks like one of those

279
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:18,480
old arcade games.

280
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,840
Did you play them as a kid?

281
00:14:22,170 --> 00:14:22,980
No.

282
00:14:23,790 --> 00:14:25,450
Then what did you play as a kid?

283
00:14:27,670 --> 00:14:29,270
I used to play with my nephew.

284
00:14:30,670 --> 00:14:32,740
What did you play with Fu Zhengchu?

285
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,770
He liked playing house.

286
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:47,720
Come here.

287
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:22,100
Should I tighten it a little more?

288
00:15:31,860 --> 00:15:32,580
Too tight?

289
00:15:35,510 --> 00:15:36,480
A little.

290
00:15:49,270 --> 00:15:49,930
Your hands.

291
00:16:13,910 --> 00:16:14,740
Pick a mode.

292
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:17,670
This game

293
00:16:17,670 --> 00:16:18,930
requires two players.

294
00:16:20,230 --> 00:16:21,940
Please select a game mode.

295
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:23,670
A. Parent-Child Mode

296
00:16:24,250 --> 00:16:24,960
Parent-child mode.

297
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:26,190
B. Couple Mode

298
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:28,320
I think this Parent-child mode

299
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,480
describes our relationship

300
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:30,370
best.

301
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:32,080
You can be the dad,

302
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:33,480
and I can be the daughter.

303
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:36,370
Or I can be the mom,

304
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:37,370
and you can be the—

305
00:16:41,010 --> 00:16:41,670
Never mind.

306
00:17:01,620 --> 00:17:03,080
The game is about to begin.

307
00:17:03,170 --> 00:17:04,440
Please get ready.

308
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:06,420
Daddy,

309
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:08,720
are you taking me on an adventure
in the woods?

310
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:10,349
That's right. Let's go!

311
00:17:20,060 --> 00:17:20,750
[Caution: obstacle ahead]

312
00:17:21,510 --> 00:17:22,140
[Swerve left]

313
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:28,010
[Swerve left]

314
00:17:29,530 --> 00:17:31,330
Hold on tight, kiddo.

315
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:31,540
[Swerve right]

316
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:32,680
Don't fall off!

317
00:17:46,210 --> 00:17:46,810
[Multiple obstacles ahead! Watch out!]

318
00:17:51,470 --> 00:17:52,390
[Swerve left. Obstacle ahead!]

319
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:57,720
[Swerve right. Obstacle ahead!]

320
00:18:00,130 --> 00:18:01,360
[Swerve left. Obstacle ahead!]

321
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:03,840
[Swerve right. Obstacle ahead!]

322
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:14,460
[Swerve left. Obstacle ahead!]

323
00:18:34,350 --> 00:18:36,410
We're about to reach the finish line.

324
00:18:51,850 --> 00:18:52,660
Was it fun?

325
00:18:55,930 --> 00:18:58,520
This mode is a little unusual.

326
00:18:59,350 --> 00:19:00,010
Unusual?

327
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:02,750
M-Maybe it's because we were
in Parent-Child Mode.

328
00:19:02,750 --> 00:19:03,700
It probably leaves out some

329
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:05,560
of the shooting actions for kids.

330
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:10,960
So you didn't get to do anything.

331
00:19:12,510 --> 00:19:13,310
Yeah.

332
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:16,010
Maybe that's just

333
00:19:16,010 --> 00:19:16,790
how Parent-Child Mode works.

334
00:19:16,790 --> 00:19:19,050
The kid just sits in the back

335
00:19:19,330 --> 00:19:20,660
and enjoys the scenery.

336
00:19:21,750 --> 00:19:22,550
Was it nice?

337
00:19:24,170 --> 00:19:25,610
It was pretty nice.

338
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:34,260
Good morning, sir.

339
00:19:35,350 --> 00:19:36,500
Look at you, young lady.

340
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:38,100
You're positively beaming.

341
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:39,900
What's got you in such a good mood?

342
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:41,420
I'm the new intern,

343
00:19:41,420 --> 00:19:42,200
Yun Li.

344
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:43,420
Have a wonderful day!

345
00:19:43,420 --> 00:19:44,620
All right, all right.

346
00:19:47,850 --> 00:19:49,910
Good things put a spring in your step.

347
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:52,070
Ah, to be young again!

348
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:31,160
Yuan.

349
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,160
Go by yourself.

350
00:20:36,590 --> 00:20:37,400
Come on, Yuan.

351
00:20:37,630 --> 00:20:38,270
Help me out.

352
00:20:38,270 --> 00:20:39,040
I don't want to.

353
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:39,870
What are you doing?

354
00:20:39,870 --> 00:20:40,800
You're the best.

355
00:20:50,830 --> 00:20:51,640
Excuse me.

356
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,130
Sorry to bother you.

357
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:57,310
M-My friend and I

358
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,000
were over there watching

359
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,160
you play with this robot

360
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:04,160
for quite a while.

361
00:21:05,240 --> 00:21:06,570
I'm not playing with it.

362
00:21:06,590 --> 00:21:07,790
I'm training it.

363
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:12,400
This robot is pretty cute.

364
00:21:13,310 --> 00:21:14,770
Did you build it yourself?

365
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:15,770
Yeah.

366
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:21,510
Why don't you try this?

367
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:28,160
I'll get going, then.

368
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:31,920
All delivered.

369
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:32,590
Come on, let's go.

370
00:21:32,590 --> 00:21:33,550
Aren't you going to say something to her?

371
00:21:33,550 --> 00:21:34,410
No, no.

372
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:35,440
Come on, let's go.

373
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:09,350
Isn't coffee his favorite?

374
00:22:09,660 --> 00:22:11,460
How come he hasn't even had a sip?

375
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:39,160
Here you go.

376
00:22:41,240 --> 00:22:42,230
Thanks.

377
00:22:43,750 --> 00:22:44,510
Didn't we agree

378
00:22:44,510 --> 00:22:45,240
to go have some fun?

379
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:46,970
How come we're back here again?

380
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:51,430
Look at that smile!
You're practically glowing.

381
00:22:51,740 --> 00:22:52,600
Come on, spill.

382
00:22:52,850 --> 00:22:54,090
First day at work,

383
00:22:54,140 --> 00:22:55,160
and did things with your dream guy

384
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:56,250
go better

385
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:58,500
than expected?

386
00:22:58,790 --> 00:23:00,240
It's not that dramatic.

387
00:23:00,440 --> 00:23:01,700
We just got a little closer

388
00:23:01,700 --> 00:23:04,330
because of work.

389
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:06,160
Just getting a tiny bit closer

390
00:23:06,160 --> 00:23:07,500
has you this excited?

391
00:23:08,750 --> 00:23:10,440
You're such a lovesick fool.

392
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:14,740
Honestly, Xia's uncle seems

393
00:23:14,740 --> 00:23:16,530
to really look out for you.

394
00:23:16,660 --> 00:23:18,720
Maybe you two actually have a chance.

395
00:23:19,660 --> 00:23:20,530
I think so, too.

396
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:22,370
He's really considerate of me.

397
00:23:26,720 --> 00:23:28,590
Uncle treats all of us
younger-generation relatives so well.

398
00:23:28,590 --> 00:23:30,030
Whenever we went out,

399
00:23:30,030 --> 00:23:30,590
he was always the one

400
00:23:30,590 --> 00:23:32,240
who'd wait in line
and pay for everything.

401
00:23:32,240 --> 00:23:33,660
When my sister and I were little,

402
00:23:33,660 --> 00:23:34,720
all we had to do was call out "Uncle,"

403
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:36,520
and we had everything we needed.

404
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:38,170
The younger generation...

405
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:39,800
The younger generation!

406
00:23:39,830 --> 00:23:40,440
Tangy,

407
00:23:40,900 --> 00:23:42,350
what if Fu Shize really sees me

408
00:23:42,350 --> 00:23:44,610
as someone from the younger generation?

409
00:23:44,750 --> 00:23:45,850
What do you mean, the younger generation?

410
00:23:45,850 --> 00:23:47,380
Aren't you two the same age?

411
00:23:48,290 --> 00:23:49,660
He skipped the rest of elementary school

412
00:23:49,660 --> 00:23:51,140
and went straight to junior high.

413
00:23:51,140 --> 00:23:52,350
So he's been surrounded by people

414
00:23:52,350 --> 00:23:54,240
older than him since he was little.

415
00:23:54,240 --> 00:23:55,850
He probably never even realized

416
00:23:55,850 --> 00:23:57,440
we're the same age.

417
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:59,240
Plus, he became an uncle

418
00:23:59,240 --> 00:24:00,200
at such a young age,

419
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:01,530
and he's always around his nephews

420
00:24:01,530 --> 00:24:02,750
and nieces.

421
00:24:02,850 --> 00:24:04,090
And since I hang out with Fu Zhengchu

422
00:24:04,090 --> 00:24:04,960
and the others,

423
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:06,750
what if he really sees me
as one of the younger generation?

424
00:24:06,750 --> 00:24:08,350
What am I supposed to do then?

425
00:24:08,900 --> 00:24:09,530
I mean,

426
00:24:09,530 --> 00:24:10,900
it's not impossible.

427
00:24:11,330 --> 00:24:13,350
You're supposed to be his girlfriend,

428
00:24:13,350 --> 00:24:14,350
so don't let some twist of fate

429
00:24:14,350 --> 00:24:16,150
turn you into his niece instead.

430
00:24:18,090 --> 00:24:19,250
Why do I feel like

431
00:24:20,010 --> 00:24:21,220
I'm getting further and further

432
00:24:21,220 --> 00:24:23,220
down the path to becoming his niece?

433
00:24:24,290 --> 00:24:25,010
Then we need to find a way

434
00:24:25,010 --> 00:24:26,270
to turn things around.

435
00:24:26,510 --> 00:24:27,310
How?

436
00:24:27,810 --> 00:24:28,610
Well...

437
00:24:29,810 --> 00:24:31,590
ask him how old he is,

438
00:24:31,590 --> 00:24:32,510
then tell him

439
00:24:32,510 --> 00:24:33,610
your birthday.

440
00:24:33,610 --> 00:24:34,350
That way, he'll realize

441
00:24:34,350 --> 00:24:35,480
you're the same age.

442
00:24:37,980 --> 00:24:39,440
Do you think that'll work?

443
00:24:39,590 --> 00:24:41,380
Whether it works or not, you have to try.

444
00:24:41,380 --> 00:24:42,700
Do you really want
to end up with another uncle?

445
00:24:42,700 --> 00:24:43,440
No way.

446
00:25:02,970 --> 00:25:05,360
[Robot Soccer Tournament]

447
00:25:06,590 --> 00:25:09,790
[XUST Football Field]

448
00:25:09,810 --> 00:25:11,590
[Specially invited by the tournament:
XUST Unique team members as team leaders.]

449
00:25:30,710 --> 00:25:31,710
Hey, Li.

450
00:25:31,740 --> 00:25:32,800
What are you doing?

451
00:25:33,030 --> 00:25:33,960
Studying.

452
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:35,590
Go to my room now

453
00:25:35,620 --> 00:25:37,010
and video call me.

454
00:25:46,660 --> 00:25:48,480
Yun Li, I'm in.

455
00:25:48,850 --> 00:25:50,580
See that wardrobe on the right?

456
00:25:50,960 --> 00:25:51,920
There's a box on top.

457
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:52,660
Do you see it?

458
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:53,480
This one?

459
00:25:54,330 --> 00:25:55,860
Yeah, yeah, that's the one.

460
00:25:58,330 --> 00:25:59,020
Wait, Yun Li,

461
00:25:59,020 --> 00:26:00,180
what's this about?

462
00:26:00,400 --> 00:26:01,740
What do you mean?

463
00:26:01,850 --> 00:26:02,950
[Open this and you're a loser]

464
00:26:02,290 --> 00:26:03,050
Just look.

465
00:26:03,330 --> 00:26:04,160
Don't worry about that.
Just open it first.

466
00:26:04,160 --> 00:26:05,150
Open it first.

467
00:26:08,410 --> 00:26:09,550
See that little robot

468
00:26:09,550 --> 00:26:11,480
I used in the competition?

469
00:26:13,100 --> 00:26:13,970
This one?

470
00:26:14,100 --> 00:26:15,330
Yeah, that's the one.

471
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:17,400
You still have this junk?

472
00:26:18,570 --> 00:26:19,000
Wait,

473
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:19,830
check if there's

474
00:26:19,830 --> 00:26:21,490
a blue envelope in there, too.

475
00:26:23,350 --> 00:26:23,940
This one?

476
00:26:23,940 --> 00:26:25,140
Yeah, that's the one.

477
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:27,240
There's also a little soccer ball.

478
00:26:27,240 --> 00:26:28,840
It should be right next to it.

479
00:26:31,350 --> 00:26:32,700
Ship all of these to me.

480
00:26:33,040 --> 00:26:33,700
Gotta go.

481
00:26:33,750 --> 00:26:34,550
Wait,

482
00:26:36,740 --> 00:26:38,070
send me 200 yuan please.

483
00:26:38,350 --> 00:26:39,350
I already sent you money last time.

484
00:26:39,350 --> 00:26:40,050
No way.

485
00:26:56,270 --> 00:26:56,740
Yuan,

486
00:26:56,850 --> 00:26:57,960
I ordered this just for you.

487
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:58,690
Give it a try.

488
00:26:59,290 --> 00:27:01,350
All right, what do you want this time?

489
00:27:01,670 --> 00:27:03,110
Yuan, here's the thing.

490
00:27:03,480 --> 00:27:04,680
My friends and I are planning

491
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:06,220
to make a little investment.

492
00:27:06,220 --> 00:27:07,510
We're just a little short on funds.

493
00:27:07,510 --> 00:27:07,940
So, I was wondering if you could...

494
00:27:07,940 --> 00:27:08,480
Are any of your friends

495
00:27:08,480 --> 00:27:09,570
even trustworthy?

496
00:27:09,570 --> 00:27:10,310
Of course!

497
00:27:10,310 --> 00:27:11,530
Totally trustworthy.

498
00:27:11,530 --> 00:27:12,420
Our investment

499
00:27:12,420 --> 00:27:14,880
is fair, reasonable, and completely legal.

500
00:27:14,920 --> 00:27:16,270
Your mom already talked to me.

501
00:27:16,270 --> 00:27:17,420
She told me not to give you any money.

502
00:27:17,420 --> 00:27:19,020
If you need money, go ask her.

503
00:27:19,290 --> 00:27:20,110
Yuan, I just—

504
00:27:20,140 --> 00:27:21,080
Don't touch me.

505
00:27:21,720 --> 00:27:22,920
Come on, do me a favor.

506
00:27:23,830 --> 00:27:25,030
No way. That's final.

507
00:27:29,940 --> 00:27:30,510
Yuan.

508
00:27:30,510 --> 00:27:31,880
I-I'll get going, then.

509
00:27:35,010 --> 00:27:35,610
Shize.

510
00:27:38,110 --> 00:27:39,270
How did I end up

511
00:27:39,270 --> 00:27:40,530
with a cousin like him?

512
00:27:43,380 --> 00:27:44,610
You dragged me out

513
00:27:45,140 --> 00:27:47,070
in the middle of the night.
What is it?

514
00:27:47,070 --> 00:27:49,070
Can't I call you out just to hang out?

515
00:27:49,610 --> 00:27:50,810
What are you drinking?

516
00:27:50,810 --> 00:27:51,530
Whiskey?

517
00:27:52,330 --> 00:27:53,830
No, I drove here.

518
00:27:54,030 --> 00:27:55,360
Get him a glass of juice.

519
00:28:02,440 --> 00:28:03,330
The Light Chaser has almost

520
00:28:03,330 --> 00:28:04,270
finished testing.

521
00:28:04,270 --> 00:28:06,640
A few more adjustments,
and it'll be ready to launch.

522
00:28:06,640 --> 00:28:08,170
I didn't ask you about that.

523
00:28:09,810 --> 00:28:10,740
Isn't that

524
00:28:10,920 --> 00:28:12,050
why you asked me out?

525
00:28:12,810 --> 00:28:13,810
Can't I just

526
00:28:13,810 --> 00:28:14,240
want to have a drink with you,

527
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:15,840
without talking about work?

528
00:28:19,810 --> 00:28:21,140
You could've done that at home.

529
00:28:21,140 --> 00:28:21,830
You've been

530
00:28:21,830 --> 00:28:22,680
so busy at the company lately.

531
00:28:22,680 --> 00:28:24,940
When would you have time
to drink at home?

532
00:28:25,180 --> 00:28:25,980
How funny.

533
00:28:29,140 --> 00:28:29,900
How's your digital twin

534
00:28:29,900 --> 00:28:30,830
coming along?

535
00:28:32,470 --> 00:28:33,270
What?

536
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:35,000
Why so secretive?

537
00:28:35,140 --> 00:28:36,400
You can't even tell me?

538
00:28:37,350 --> 00:28:38,500
You wouldn't understand
even if I told you.

539
00:28:38,500 --> 00:28:39,070
You haven't even told me.

540
00:28:39,070 --> 00:28:40,700
How do you know I wouldn't understand?

541
00:28:40,700 --> 00:28:41,700
Have you forgotten

542
00:28:41,700 --> 00:28:43,140
how you and Jiang Yuan

543
00:28:43,140 --> 00:28:44,140
came to me back then

544
00:28:44,140 --> 00:28:45,070
to ask about two research areas:

545
00:28:45,070 --> 00:28:46,070
artificial intelligence (AI)

546
00:28:46,070 --> 00:28:47,590
and intelligent automation?

547
00:28:47,590 --> 00:28:48,270
I even went

548
00:28:48,270 --> 00:28:49,440
and studied

549
00:28:49,440 --> 00:28:50,680
the differences between them
because of you.

550
00:28:50,680 --> 00:28:52,210
How could I not understand?

551
00:29:00,640 --> 00:29:01,440
By the way,

552
00:29:01,440 --> 00:29:02,030
isn't Great-Aunt's birthday

553
00:29:02,030 --> 00:29:03,380
coming up soon?

554
00:29:04,420 --> 00:29:05,180
You hardly ever

555
00:29:05,180 --> 00:29:06,440
get to see each other,

556
00:29:06,480 --> 00:29:07,310
so you should make a good impression

557
00:29:07,310 --> 00:29:08,810
while you have the chance.

558
00:29:10,380 --> 00:29:11,050
Got it.

559
00:30:57,460 --> 00:30:58,180
I...

560
00:31:25,290 --> 00:31:25,900
Hello.

561
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:27,660
Who is it?

562
00:31:34,620 --> 00:31:35,990
This is my seat.

563
00:31:37,640 --> 00:31:38,740
Ms. Idle Cloud,

564
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:40,200
they said

565
00:31:40,200 --> 00:31:41,140
our internship schedules

566
00:31:41,140 --> 00:31:42,090
are different,

567
00:31:42,180 --> 00:31:43,830
so whoever's here for work can sit here.

568
00:31:43,830 --> 00:31:45,900
What if our shifts overlap?

569
00:31:48,700 --> 00:31:50,500
Mr. Qin said you're nice

570
00:31:50,830 --> 00:31:52,760
and wouldn't fight me for the seat.

571
00:31:53,880 --> 00:31:54,680
Oh,

572
00:31:55,500 --> 00:31:57,240
and I haven't touched your stuff,

573
00:31:57,240 --> 00:31:58,040
so don't touch

574
00:31:58,090 --> 00:31:59,240
mine either.

575
00:32:01,200 --> 00:32:03,060
You sure like to play by the rules.

576
00:32:03,330 --> 00:32:04,140
Yeah.

577
00:32:06,940 --> 00:32:09,140
I thought you interviewed

578
00:32:09,140 --> 00:32:11,380
for an internship
in the engineering department.

579
00:32:11,380 --> 00:32:13,840
Why are you
in the publicity department too?

580
00:32:13,940 --> 00:32:15,070
Didn't make the cut?

581
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:19,270
Don't be too upset.

582
00:32:19,900 --> 00:32:21,830
We're all just working
for a living, after all.

583
00:32:21,830 --> 00:32:23,400
If you don't have what it takes,

584
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:25,460
you shouldn't be in this line of work.

585
00:32:27,110 --> 00:32:28,310
Feifei, you're here.

586
00:32:29,420 --> 00:32:30,290
Mr. Qin.

587
00:32:32,140 --> 00:32:32,750
Yun Li,

588
00:32:32,750 --> 00:32:34,010
I forgot to tell you.

589
00:32:34,220 --> 00:32:34,980
Feifei

590
00:32:35,010 --> 00:32:36,290
is interning here too.

591
00:32:36,770 --> 00:32:38,030
I think today is the only day

592
00:32:38,030 --> 00:32:39,550
you'll be working the same shift.

593
00:32:39,550 --> 00:32:40,310
There's also

594
00:32:40,310 --> 00:32:41,500
seating in the break area,

595
00:32:41,500 --> 00:32:44,160
so you two can figure out
how to divide things up.

596
00:32:44,350 --> 00:32:45,290
Mr. Qin,

597
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:47,290
Yun Li is nice.

598
00:32:47,750 --> 00:32:49,480
You won't fight me for the seat,

599
00:32:49,500 --> 00:32:50,550
will you, Yun Li?

600
00:32:52,110 --> 00:32:53,110
Actually, I will.

601
00:32:53,750 --> 00:32:54,660
This is my seat.

602
00:32:54,660 --> 00:32:56,390
I'd appreciate it if you moved.

603
00:33:00,310 --> 00:33:01,010
Yun Li...

604
00:33:01,010 --> 00:33:01,590
Ms. Fang assigned

605
00:33:01,590 --> 00:33:02,720
this seat to me.

606
00:33:02,750 --> 00:33:04,010
If there's going to be
any change in seating arrangements,

607
00:33:04,010 --> 00:33:06,270
please have Ms. Fang inform me directly.

608
00:33:07,250 --> 00:33:08,050
Feifei,

609
00:33:08,460 --> 00:33:10,310
I can't believe this new intern

610
00:33:10,600 --> 00:33:12,060
is being so unreasonable.

611
00:33:12,610 --> 00:33:14,140
I'll find you another seat.

612
00:33:20,110 --> 00:33:21,250
Pick up your things,

613
00:33:23,430 --> 00:33:24,280
new intern.

614
00:33:37,720 --> 00:33:38,510
Yun Li,

615
00:33:38,980 --> 00:33:40,040
you did great.

616
00:33:40,060 --> 00:33:42,110
You did the right thing.

617
00:33:52,160 --> 00:33:53,720
Why do people

618
00:33:53,720 --> 00:33:55,250
keep throwing their weight

619
00:33:55,250 --> 00:33:57,700
around in this office?

620
00:33:58,590 --> 00:34:00,050
That little girl was the one

621
00:34:00,050 --> 00:34:01,290
who got there first

622
00:34:01,290 --> 00:34:02,090
and took the seat.

623
00:34:02,090 --> 00:34:03,960
Why try to take it from her?

624
00:34:04,700 --> 00:34:08,230
Don't they understand
the concept of first come, first served?

625
00:35:05,900 --> 00:35:06,900
Your cup's full.

626
00:35:11,900 --> 00:35:13,550
I'll get a tissue.

627
00:35:34,610 --> 00:35:35,420
You...

628
00:35:35,670 --> 00:35:37,760
This coffee smells really good.

629
00:35:38,960 --> 00:35:39,760
Want some?

630
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:41,530
Yeah.

631
00:35:46,780 --> 00:35:47,610
Sugar?

632
00:35:51,170 --> 00:35:52,970
Do you like sugar in your coffee?

633
00:35:53,280 --> 00:35:53,980
No.

634
00:35:54,820 --> 00:35:56,010
Then I don't either.

635
00:35:58,360 --> 00:35:59,670
I really don't.

636
00:36:05,480 --> 00:36:06,110
Thanks.

637
00:36:14,550 --> 00:36:15,600
How can anyone

638
00:36:15,630 --> 00:36:17,760
drink something that tastes this bad?

639
00:36:22,860 --> 00:36:23,650
I-I...

640
00:36:23,650 --> 00:36:25,860
I think I'll add some sugar after all.

641
00:36:29,030 --> 00:36:30,230
"Then I don't either.

642
00:36:31,590 --> 00:36:32,780
I really don't."

643
00:36:36,010 --> 00:36:36,610
I...

644
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:49,130
Go ahead if you want.

645
00:36:54,880 --> 00:36:56,480
I just want to see

646
00:36:56,480 --> 00:36:58,380
what this different-flavored coffee

647
00:36:58,380 --> 00:36:59,530
tastes like.

648
00:37:26,840 --> 00:37:27,630
Yun Li.

649
00:37:29,320 --> 00:37:29,920
Come here.

650
00:37:32,800 --> 00:37:33,690
Mr. Qin,

651
00:37:33,690 --> 00:37:34,780
what is it?

652
00:37:35,780 --> 00:37:36,780
I'm going to meet a client

653
00:37:36,780 --> 00:37:37,800
with Feifei later.

654
00:37:37,800 --> 00:37:38,590
You

655
00:37:38,780 --> 00:37:40,380
move all of this over there

656
00:37:40,570 --> 00:37:42,100
and get it done before noon.

657
00:37:42,630 --> 00:37:44,050
Before noon?

658
00:37:44,050 --> 00:37:45,800
How is that even possible?

659
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:47,630
There's so much stuff.

660
00:37:47,630 --> 00:37:48,880
There's no way I'll finish by noon.

661
00:37:48,880 --> 00:37:50,540
Then finish it before you eat.

662
00:37:50,690 --> 00:37:51,730
Work comes first.

663
00:37:53,420 --> 00:37:54,420
Let's go, Feifei.

664
00:37:59,000 --> 00:37:59,980
This intern's going

665
00:37:59,980 --> 00:38:01,640
to have a hard time from now on.

666
00:38:01,780 --> 00:38:03,110
She crossed Qin Haigou,

667
00:38:03,110 --> 00:38:04,970
so she's in for a world of trouble.

668
00:38:20,440 --> 00:38:21,480
Aren't you going to lunch, Yun Li?

669
00:38:21,480 --> 00:38:22,920
The boxed meals will be gone soon.

670
00:38:22,920 --> 00:38:23,970
It's fine. I'm almost done.

671
00:38:23,970 --> 00:38:24,690
Go ahead.

672
00:38:24,690 --> 00:38:25,340
All right.

673
00:38:34,190 --> 00:38:35,630
Why bother?

674
00:38:36,130 --> 00:38:37,530
The food's already cold—

675
00:38:45,260 --> 00:38:46,410
Have you eaten?

676
00:38:47,280 --> 00:38:48,030
Yes.

677
00:38:48,300 --> 00:38:49,500
I've eaten too.

678
00:38:51,300 --> 00:38:53,440
So, what are you doing here?

679
00:38:53,880 --> 00:38:54,810
Getting coffee.

680
00:39:17,380 --> 00:39:19,230
H-Has he really eaten?

681
00:39:37,890 --> 00:39:38,890
Hello.

682
00:39:41,500 --> 00:39:42,460
Room 8001?

683
00:39:42,460 --> 00:39:43,010
One moment, please.

684
00:39:43,010 --> 00:39:44,130
I'll bring it to your room shortly.

685
00:39:44,130 --> 00:39:44,780
Xia,

686
00:39:44,780 --> 00:39:46,710
did your brother go to class today?

687
00:39:47,260 --> 00:39:47,940
He did.

688
00:39:58,820 --> 00:40:00,640
♪ Sitting by the window ♪

689
00:40:00,660 --> 00:40:03,010
♪ Watching the afternoon breeze ♪

690
00:40:03,030 --> 00:40:05,270
♪ Clouds like cotton candy ♪

691
00:40:05,300 --> 00:40:07,260
♪ Lining up in secret ♪

692
00:40:07,290 --> 00:40:09,420
♪ I turn my headphones up ♪

693
00:40:09,440 --> 00:40:11,420
♪ As loud as they can go ♪

694
00:40:11,530 --> 00:40:13,510
♪ Listening to my own heartbeat ♪

695
00:40:13,670 --> 00:40:15,510
♪ Something feels a little strange ♪

696
00:40:15,530 --> 00:40:16,160
Xia,

697
00:40:16,340 --> 00:40:17,870
is your brother out of class yet?

698
00:40:17,870 --> 00:40:19,930
♪ What's happening to me? ♪

699
00:40:19,950 --> 00:40:22,020
♪ I can't find the remote ♪

700
00:40:20,260 --> 00:40:21,460
How would I know?

701
00:40:22,050 --> 00:40:24,280
♪ What's happening to me now? ♪

702
00:40:24,310 --> 00:40:26,330
♪ My heart suddenly skips a beat ♪

703
00:40:26,350 --> 00:40:27,920
♪ A little anxious ♪

704
00:40:27,690 --> 00:40:28,380
Is Fu Zhengchu

705
00:40:27,950 --> 00:40:29,420
♪ A little curious ♪

706
00:40:28,380 --> 00:40:29,900
going skateboarding today, then?

707
00:40:29,440 --> 00:40:31,560
♪ My whole world is you ♪

708
00:40:31,590 --> 00:40:32,480
♪ Oh my, oh my ♪

709
00:40:32,510 --> 00:40:34,180
♪ This little craziness ♪

710
00:40:34,200 --> 00:40:36,780
♪ Feels a little sweet ♪

711
00:40:35,210 --> 00:40:36,530
Ask him yourself.

712
00:40:38,280 --> 00:40:40,190
If I could ask him in person,

713
00:40:40,190 --> 00:40:41,590
why would I be asking you?

714
00:40:43,170 --> 00:40:45,890
♪ Your little universe ♪

715
00:40:46,910 --> 00:40:48,910
♪ Will always come to you ♪

716
00:40:58,320 --> 00:41:00,280
Mr. Qin is the worst.

717
00:41:00,280 --> 00:41:01,610
He won't even let me eat!

718
00:41:03,940 --> 00:41:05,190
He never does

719
00:41:05,220 --> 00:41:06,660
a single decent thing.

720
00:41:11,330 --> 00:41:12,530
How could EAW

721
00:41:12,560 --> 00:41:14,040
hire someone like him?
